          </ownedRelationship>
          <ownedRelationship xsi:type="sysml:OwningMembership" xmi:id="2cd7742a-f898-59c5-bab3-b9e0a7b03b10" elementId="2cd7742a-f898-59c5-bab3-b9e0a7b03b10">
            <ownedRelatedElement xsi:type="sysml:Documentation" xmi:id="b7ef799d-22ae-5ecd-ad43-0e75753695f0" elementId="b7ef799d-22ae-5ecd-ad43-0e75753695f0" body="source: item 5-20.4 Helmholtz energy, Helmholtz function&#xA;symbol(s): `A`, `F`&#xA;application domain: generic&#xA;name: HelmholtzEnergy (specializes Energy)&#xA;quantity dimension: L^2*M^1*T^-2&#xA;measurement unit(s): J, kg*m^2*s^-2&#xA;tensor order: 0&#xA;definition: difference of internal energy of the system and the product of thermodynamic temperature and entropy of the system: `A = U - TS` where `U` is internal energy (item 5-20.2), `T` is thermodynamic temperature (item 5-1), and `S` is entropy (item 5-18)&#xA;remarks: The name Helmholtz free energy is also used. However, this term is not recommended.&#xA;"/>
          </ownedRelationship>
        </ownedRelatedElement>
      </ownedRelationship>
